      <section class="faq" aria-labelledby="libraryiq-faq-heading">
        <h2 id="libraryiq-faq-heading">Frequently asked</h2>
        <details>
          <summary>What is LibraryIQ?</summary>
          <p>A reading tracker and personal library manager that runs at <a href="https://libraryiq.inknironapps.com" rel="noopener">libraryiq.inknironapps.com</a>. It is a web app, so there is nothing to download — open the link, sign in with Google, and your library is there. It can also be installed to a phone or desktop home screen and then behaves like any other app.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need to install anything?</summary>
          <p>No. LibraryIQ runs in any modern browser. If you want it on your home screen, use your browser's <em>Install</em> or <em>Add to Home Screen</em> option — it then opens full screen, keeps working offline, and updates itself.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is there still an Android app?</summary>
          <p>No. The Android alpha has been replaced by the web app, which does more and runs everywhere. On Android, open <a href="https://libraryiq.inknironapps.com" rel="noopener">libraryiq.inknironapps.com</a> in Chrome and choose <em>Install app</em> — you get a home-screen icon, full-screen launch, offline support and the camera barcode scanner, with no store install required.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What does LibraryIQ cost?</summary>
          <p>The app is free. Unlimited books, every view, cross-device sync, barcode scanning and export cost nothing. Only AI requests are metered: the free plan includes 20 a month, and paid plans run from Reader at $5/month for 1,000 requests up to Institution at $100/month for 20,000. Barcode scanning is never counted against an allowance.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use my own AI key instead of subscribing?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Paste an Anthropic, OpenAI, Google or xAI key under <em>AI features</em> and the AI tools run unlimited on your own account with nothing counted against an allowance.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does it work offline?</summary>
          <p>Yes. The browser keeps a local mirror of your library, so it opens and edits offline. Changes queue up, survive a reload, and replay when you reconnect. Metadata lookup and AI features need a connection.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where does my data live, and can I get it out?</summary>
          <p>In your own account on LibraryIQ's server, mirrored locally in your browser. Export gives you a full JSON backup or a CSV — either the complete spreadsheet or the narrower shape the Goodreads importer accepts. Deleting your account permanently erases it and everything in it.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I bring my library over from Goodreads?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Settings takes a Goodreads CSV export and merges it into what you already have, matching on ISBN, title and author so nothing arrives twice.</p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <aside class="related" aria-labelledby="libraryiq-related-heading">
        <h2 id="libraryiq-related-heading">More from the workshop</h2>
